{
 "_note": "seg_15 code parts, each drawing in its own px (web/lib/parts.js; 根因清单 2026-11-21 「笔芯和笔不对了……吉他弦和吉他不是一块的」). lan.ends: where the drawn lanyard strands stop and code hangs the lower strands and the empty clip (lan.under: no strap drawn above, the strand comes out from under a drawn edge); len: the clip's drop below the ends (m, before the layer scale); kid: 小林 そうた's stubs. Measured on crops (work/seg/15/parts/), checked by check_ends.py and PART AUDIT in seg_15.js. Her strings are no longer drawn by code (2026-11-21 third round: only the strings Codex drew). 2026-11-22 (third review MUST 'the lanyard and the drawing are not one piece'): sty = the drawn strand's own width w, outline o, outline colour oc, core colour cc (null: a solid strand), dots (the core's screen) in drawing px, dirs = the drawn strand's direction at each end; code continues each strand along its dirs with that width, outline and core (seg_15.js clip()), starting inside the drawn strand so its cut cap is covered. class 'cased': PART AUDIT checks both drawn outline edges at the end. Measured with work/seg/15/fix5/measure_cords.py and profile.py; t15_p1h2(+_turn), f15_n4_bg newly registered (their strands were cut square, no clip). f15_p6_a/f15_p6c/f15_p6_c2: the strands end in white square fittings (cap bottoms measured on each drawing); code hangs the empty clip from them (class light: the strand is pale teal, checked as opaque). 2026-11-22 fourth round (review r3 MUST: t01_p7/t15_p7_turn still fell back to the plain solid teal line): EVERY lan has sty + dirs (clip() has no default any more; a lan without sty is a PART AUDIT problem and throws when drawn). sty.ground 'dark': the strand lies on a ground of its outline's colour (the style audit cannot see its outer edge there); sty.fit: the drawn piece at the end is a fitting (code leaves its bottom edge; sty is the strand above it); sty.ov: how far (drawing px) code starts inside the drawn end. under entries: no strand drawn, sty = the film's cased lanyard in that drawing's ink. Measured with work/seg/15/fix6/measure2.py, rows.py, regprof.py.",
